# Debian postinst — Default Apps hint

electron-builder already emits a `.desktop` with `MimeType` for `sms` / `smsto` / `tel` / `callto` / `im` / `mms`. After `apt install`, users may still need to pick the handler once.

Suggested `postinst` snippet (do not run as root against another user's defaults):

```
xdg-mime default com.edwardlthompson.google-messages.desktop x-scheme-handler/sms || true
xdg-mime default com.edwardlthompson.google-messages.desktop x-scheme-handler/smsto || true
xdg-mime default com.edwardlthompson.google-messages.desktop x-scheme-handler/tel || true
echo "If links still open the browser, set Default Apps in GNOME/KDE Settings."
```

The first-run Defaults panel is the supported UX; this hint is for distro packages only.
